    {
      "type": 1,
      "name": "DiagnosisHeading",
      "content": {
        "json": "## Throttling diagnosis \u2014 disk limit or VM SKU limit?\n\nThese four charts show the peak consumed percentage over the selected time range for every selected VM. A series at or above 95% for five consecutive minutes indicates throttling at that scope.\n\n* **A DISK chart reaches ~100%** \u2192 an individual data disk hit its own provisioned IOPS or bandwidth limit \u2192 resize or upgrade that disk.\n* **A VM SKU chart reaches ~100%** \u2192 the VM hit its aggregate IOPS or bandwidth limit across all disks \u2192 resize the VM.\n* **Both high** \u2192 the disk is saturating and rolling up to the VM limit too.\n\nUse the detailed trend charts below to see when it happened and which LUN."
      }
    },
